import ZInQKernel.Contrib.OneProof.RC.ModelGeneric6.SeamLift
import ZInQKernel.Contrib.OneProof.RC.ModelGeneric6.Cyclicity
import ZInQKernel.Contrib.OneProof.RC.ModelGeneric4.Homothety
import ZInQKernel.Contrib.OneProof.RC.ModelGeneric5.ComplexPoints
import ZInQKernel.Contrib.OneProof.RC.AtkinRational.Matrix

/-! # The moduli action of `W_Q` at complex points (generic5's item 3, over `ℂ`)

For a complex pair `(E, C)` whose class is `analyticCyclicPair τ`, and for **every** seam
`g : E(ℂ) →+ E'(ℂ)` with kernel `C_Q = (N/Q) • C`, where `E' = E.cyclicQuotientCurve C_Q Q` is the
actual vendored Vélu composite, the class of `(E', g(E[Q] ⊔ C))` is
`analyticCyclicPair (W_Q τ)` (`atkinPair_complex`). With `rationalPoints_atkinRat_complex`
(generic5) this is the choice-free target theorem at complex points
(`rationalPoints_atkinRat_complex_moduli`): `rationalPoints (y ∘ atkinRat)` is the class of
`(E', g(E[Q] ⊔ C))` for every representative `(E, C)` of `rationalPoints y` and every seam `g`.

Route. The seam, conjugated by the variable-change seams of `VariableChangeSeam`, is a seam
between period curves and lifts to `z ↦ αz` (`exists_lift_of_seam`). Its kernel `⟨τ, 1/Q⟩`
gives `L₂ = α(ℤτ + ℤ/Q)`; the Atkin–Lehner matrix with entries `Qa, b, QMc, Qd`
(`Q(ad) - M(bc) = 1`, `M = N/Q`) gives `ℤτ + ℤ/Q = ω₂(ℤ W_Qτ + ℤ)` with `ω₂ = Mcτ + d`, and
`ω₂/N = cτ/Q + d/N` generates `⟨τ/Q, 1/N⟩` modulo `ℤτ + ℤ/Q`. The homothety lemma then gives the
class. Background: Silverman, *The Arithmetic of Elliptic Curves*, 2nd ed., 2009, VI.3.6 and
VI.4.1; Diamond–Shurman, *A First Course in Modular Forms*, 2005, §1.5; Atkin–Lehner,
Math. Ann. 185 (1970) for the matrix (all UNVERIFIED). The moduli form of `W_Q` itself is
ON THE SPOT (c). -/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option maxHeartbeats 2000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option linter.style.haveILetI false

noncomputable section

open AlgebraicCurve WeierstrassCurve WeierstrassCurve.Affine WeierstrassCurve.ModelLevels
